The following parts of lib/engine.js are derived from open-code-review. Every
one of them is MODIFIED: the upstream logic is generalised out of the
code-review domain into domain-neutral primitives that are parameterised by a
domain pack, and the file/function names below are the upstream origins, not a
description of the current code.

  normalizeLine, normalizeExcerpt
      <- internal/diff/resolver.go (normalizeLine)

  matchConsecutive, anchorInDocument
      <- internal/diff/resolver.go (matchConsecutive, ResolveComment)

  resolveAnchor and its three-tier degradation ladder
      <- internal/diff/resolver.go (RelocateAcrossFiles) and
         internal/agent/relocation.go (RE_LOCATION_TASK)
      Deviation: upstream's third tier is an LLM-driven re-location. It is
      deliberately NOT reproduced. This port ends the ladder at "unanchored"
      because an anchor a model guessed is not an anchor an engine can verify.

  DEFAULT_GATE_PREDICATES and their ordering
      <- internal/agent/selection.go (selectFiles, whyExcluded)

  DEFAULT_EXCLUDE_PATTERNS
      <- internal/config/default_exclude_patterns.json

  DEFAULT_SECRET_PATTERNS
      <- internal/config/default_secret_patterns.json

  BUNDLE_DEFAULTS (minFiles, lineThreshold, maxPerBundle)
      <- internal/agent/grouping.go (GROUPING_MIN_FILES,
         GROUPING_BUNDLE_LINE_THRESHOLD, maxFilesPerGroup)

  BUDGET_DEFAULTS
      <- internal/agent/estimate.go (avgMainRoundsPerFile),
         internal/tool/file_read.go (fileReadMaxLines),
         internal/tool/git_grep.go (gitGrepMaxCount)

  critique, runCritiquePanel and the asymmetric loss orientation
      <- internal/prompts/review_filter_task_system.md (the precision-first
         "when your evidence falls short of proof, approve" policy) and the
         protected-subject veto in review_filter_task_user.md

  coverage and report
      <- internal/delegate/* (the coverage self-proof field set)

Everything else is original to this project and has no counterpart upstream:
the domain registry (lib/registry.js), the nineteen domain packs
(lib/domains.js), the on-demand tool activation lifecycle and the service
facade (index.js), the recall-first loss orientation, and the test suites.
